  "description": "Tom Ritchey built his first road frame 40 years ago in his parent's garage, and went on to bring numerous innovations to the craft. The beautiful result of all of Tom's countless hours in the saddle and mastery of his craft, the Road Logic WCS carries many of the subtleties and details gleaned from his vast experience with steel frames.\n\nTom designed an all-new, heat-treated and triple-butted Ritchey Logic tubeset for the new Road Logic WCS, featuring aggressively short-butted sections optimized for TIG welding that save weight and improve ride quality. Ritchey's forged-and-machined integrated head tube uses standard drop-in bearings which saves 80 grams over a standard head tube design.\n\nOutfitted with an Ultegra build, the Road Logic WCS also features a Ritchey WCS Curve, C-220 WCS Stem, and WCS seatpost. With a Ritchey Carbon Fork, room for wider road tires and classic Ritchey geometry, the Road Logic WCS is ideally suited for long, epic days in the saddle on roads that are not always paved. Yet it's still nimble and stiff enough to take the county line sprint at the end of the day.\n\nHeat-treated and triple-butted Ritchey Logic tubeset\n\nFits tires up to 700x28c (depending on make and model)\n\nForged and machined tapered head tube",
